1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,999
Every day, people send cryptocurrency to wallets they know
little about.

2
00:00:05,249 --> 00:00:09,482
And when something goes wrong, getting that money back may be
impossible.

3
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:13,877
Meet TxGuard.

4
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:22,038
A Web3 recipient-checking tool that helps you understand
available wallet risk evidence before sending your crypto.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,518
Choose a blockchain, enter a public wallet address, and run a
scan.

6
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:35,437
TxGuard retrieves available security intelligence and blockchain
activity, with missing coverage kept visible.

7
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:45,407
Review the findings, their sources, and the limits of the check
in plain English.

8
00:00:45,657 --> 00:00:49,477
Available explanations stay grounded in retrieved evidence.

9
00:00:49,727 --> 00:00:51,923
No assessment can guarantee safety.

10
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:00,709
Five networks: Ethereum, BNB Chain, Solana, Bitcoin, and Stacks.

11
00:01:00,959 --> 00:01:03,172
Security coverage varies by network.

12
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,530
Inspect an existing scan record on Stacks Mainnet.

13
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:13,205
A public receipt records an assertion; it does not certify the
score.

14
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:21,508
Built for P2P traders, freelancers, and everyday crypto users.

15
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,935
TxGuard. Know before you send.
